# The Dockerfile only ever COPYs app/ (and app/webapp/ for the frontend build stage) — everything
# else here is platform orchestration (hooks/, docker-compose.yml, app.json), runtime-mounted data
# (blueprint/demo-docs, storage — both bind-mounted, never baked in), or local scratch (ci-artifacts).
# Without this file `bbox run --build` had to walk all 148M/thousands of files under apps/indox/ on
# every invocation just to find the ~450K actually relevant to app/ — the dominant cost of adding
# `--build` to bbox run (see bbox's own comment on that flag).
*
!app/
!app/**

# The REAL cost, found by measuring rather than guessing: not the byte count (441KB, same before
# and after the excludes above — barely moved the timing) but the FILE count. app/webapp/node_modules
# is a local host copy the Dockerfile never reads (its own `RUN npm install` builds a fresh one
# inside the image) and app/**/__pycache__ is never read either — together thousands of small files,
# and each one costs a syscall round-trip on WSL's /mnt/c. Excluding them is what actually moves the
# number: a same-context rebuild on this platform.
app/webapp/node_modules
**/__pycache__
